# The flavours differ only in the name of the root daemon's SELinux domain -
# KernelSU labels it "ksu", APatch "su". @ROOT_DOMAIN@ is substituted at build
# time, so a rule change lands in both at once. Any other mention of that
# domain below must use the placeholder too, or the two drift apart again.

type zygisk_file file_type
typeattribute zygisk_file mlstrustedobject

# INFO: Every domain, not zygote alone: on HyperOS applications are forked by
#       hyos_spawner, so the spawner and every app it starts sit outside the
#       zygote domain and hold their own end of this socket. A zygote-only rule
#       leaves them unable to connect - a HyperOS runtime that loads nothing.
allow domain zygisk_file dir {search getattr}
allow domain zygisk_file sock_file {read write getattr open}

# INFO: "map" and "execute" on top of "read open": the loader mmaps and dlopens
#       module libraries arriving as unlabeled memfds where tmpfs is unlabelled.
allow zygote unlabeled file {getattr read open map execute}
allow zygote zygote capability sys_chroot

# INFO: To allow setns on the zygote's child mount namespace. KernelSU renamed
#       this context from su to ksu.
allow zygote @ROOT_DOMAIN@ dir search
allow zygote @ROOT_DOMAIN@ {lnk_file file} read

# INFO: The directory stays searchable from outside the zygote - the daemon
#       resolves each module library under /data/adb before handing it over as
#       a descriptor. The "file *" grant below stays zygote-only: nothing
#       outside it opens module libraries by path any more.
allow domain adb_data_file dir search
allow zygote adb_data_file file *
allow zygote proc file {read open}
allow zygote nsfs file {read open}
allow zygote zygote process execmem
allow system_server system_server process execmem
allow zygote tmpfs file *

# INFO: The same tmpfs memfds, for the processes HyperOS runs outside zygote.
#       Kept to what a dlopen performs rather than a wildcard, since this one is
#       not limited to zygote.
allow domain tmpfs file {open getattr map read execute}
allow zygote appdomain_tmpfs file *

# INFO: Zygisk Next libraries travel as memfds created by the daemon, so they
#       carry its own domain label and dlopen needs "execute" from whichever
#       process loads the module. On the memfd's type on purpose: "allow * *
#       file execute" also grants untrusted_app execute on dex2oat_exec, which
#       is what makes LSPosed/Vector report its dex2oat wrapper as unsupported.
#       Subject stays "*" because per-application targets are dlopened inside
#       the app itself, so the executing domain cannot be enumerated here.
#
#       The wildcard target does widen this to every file the daemon's domain
#       labels, not only memfds. Narrowing it is left undone deliberately: the
#       obvious spelling, "neverallow * @ROOT_DOMAIN@ dex2oat_exec file
#       execute", names a type GSI and several vendor policies do not define,
#       and a rule naming an undefined type is a hard compile error - the whole
#       policy then fails to load and nothing can be dlopened at all.
allow * @ROOT_DOMAIN@ file execute

# INFO: How a memfd gets labelled depends on the kernel, and no two cases share
#       a type. GKI gives an anonymous tmpfs inode, already covered for zygote
#       above while the companion had nothing at all. Other kernels label it
#       `unlabeled`, where zygote had only `read open` - enough to take the
#       descriptor and still fail the mmap that dlopen performs. Android 17
#       QPR1 and later label it through security_inode_init_security_anon() as
#       the creating task's SID under the new `memfd_file` class, which neither
#       tmpfs nor unlabeled matches, so every SCM_RIGHTS transfer is dropped.
#       Without these the loader receives nothing for ReadZnModules while
#       descriptor-free actions such as GetProcessFlags keep working - a
#       failure that looks like a matching problem rather than a permission one.
#
#       NOTE: no statement terminators in these comments. The policy parser
#       splits on one before it strips comments, so a single occurrence here
#       truncates the comment and hands the remainder to the rule parser,
#       which rejects it and the installer then refuses the whole module.
allow zygote @ROOT_DOMAIN@ memfd_file {getattr read write map execute}

# INFO: The same grant for the HyperOS domains, which receive those memfds.
allow domain @ROOT_DOMAIN@ memfd_file {getattr read write map execute}

allow @ROOT_DOMAIN@ @ROOT_DOMAIN@ memfd_file {getattr read write map execute}
allow @ROOT_DOMAIN@ tmpfs file {getattr read write map execute}
allow @ROOT_DOMAIN@ unlabeled file {getattr read write map execute}